        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Southwell, Nottinghamshire, England, Truro, Cornwall\n- Organizations: Southwell Minster, Truro Cathedral, Church of England\n- People: Rev. John Thomas Becher\n- Roles: English clergyman, social reformer, Vicar-General\n\nFacts:\n- Rev. John Thomas Becher was born in 1770 and died in 1848.\n- Rev. John Thomas Becher was an English clergyman, a social reformer, and Vicar-General of Southwell Minster from 1818 to 1840.\n- Southwell Minster is a minster and cathedral in Southwell, Nottinghamshire, England.\n- Truro Cathedral, formally the Cathedral of the Blessed Virgin Mary, Truro, is a Church of England cathedral in Truro, Cornwall.",
